Description: Provides easy access to reference white matter tractography
    atlases for benchmarking and anomaly detection studies of brain
    microstructure. Two datasets are available: (1) the HCP1065
    population-averaged tractography atlas with 87 white matter bundles
    derived from 1,065 Human Connectome Project (HCP) Young Adult subjects
    (Yeh 2022, distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0); and (2) per-subject TractSeg
    white matter bundle segmentations of 72 tracts in 105 HCP Young Adult
    subjects (Wasserthal et al. 2018, distributed under CC BY-NC 4.0 --
    non-commercial use only). Both datasets originate from the HCP and are
    subject to the applicable HCP data-use terms. The data are hosted as
    releases in the package's GitHub repository and are downloaded on demand
    as R 'fiber' bundle objects; no data files are bundled with the package
    itself. The package code is distributed under the MIT license; the
    underlying atlas data remain under their respective Creative Commons
    licenses.
